1
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:50,680
Here, Dad.

2
00:01:53,799 --> 00:01:55,359
Why do you think he did it?

3
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:57,439
What?

4
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:58,760
Why did he do what?

5
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:02,000
A perfectly good job...

6
00:02:03,079 --> 00:02:04,439
Why would he just quit?

7
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,519
He even made section chief.

8
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,479
And he just threw it away.

9
00:02:09,159 --> 00:02:10,599
Xiuming usually

10
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,400
deals with all sorts of people.

11
00:02:12,759 --> 00:02:13,960
Who knows who he ran into

12
00:02:14,439 --> 00:02:15,159
that egged him on?

13
00:02:15,599 --> 00:02:17,240
He's always acted on impulse,

14
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,960
and this time he probably did

15
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:20,000
something really foolish.

16
00:02:20,479 --> 00:02:21,719
Don't you worry,

17
00:02:22,039 --> 00:02:23,240
and don't be angry.

18
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,080
Tomorrow,

19
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:25,840
I'll go have a talk with him.

20
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:27,680
You?

21
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,199
Talk about what?

22
00:02:29,719 --> 00:02:31,000
I'll teach him how to conduct himself.

23
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,800
He's been lecturing you your whole life.

24
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,879
When have you ever talked sense into him?

25
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:41,360
Fair point.

26
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:44,520
Then why do you think he did it, Dad?

27
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,240
You don't think...

28
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:48,680
his wife complained about his pay?

29
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:51,319
Egged on by those Yangs, maybe?

30
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:56,199
None of you gives me any peace!

31
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,120
Right, not a single one.

32
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:02,919
Before I came over,

33
00:03:03,319 --> 00:03:05,479
I already chewed out Wen Jiayin.

34
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:07,199
You?

35
00:03:08,919 --> 00:03:10,479
Who knows which of you yelled at whom!

36
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,039
I really did!

37
00:03:13,439 --> 00:03:14,800
The thing is, before this,

38
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:15,800
I wasn't... wasn't aware.

39
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,639
If I'd known about this...

40
00:03:17,639 --> 00:03:18,879
What could you have done if you knew?

41
00:03:19,599 --> 00:03:20,800
You chose to marry her.

42
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,120
Can you even control her?

43
00:03:23,039 --> 00:03:24,439
You were put in charge of the site,

44
00:03:24,879 --> 00:03:26,000
but you have no backbone.

45
00:03:26,599 --> 00:03:28,520
That supervisor nitpicked

46
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,520
and refused to release the funds.

47
00:03:31,479 --> 00:03:32,759
Qingyou told me

48
00:03:32,759 --> 00:03:34,000
it was your wife

49
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:35,919
dragging our third boy along

50
00:03:36,719 --> 00:03:37,680
who finally secured the payout!

51
00:03:38,759 --> 00:03:40,240
What are you even good for?

52
00:03:40,599 --> 00:03:41,560
"If you'd known"?

53
00:03:41,919 --> 00:03:42,840
Known what?

54
00:03:48,159 --> 00:03:48,599
You're down.

55
00:03:49,879 --> 00:03:51,000
Number Four and I cleaned up a bit.

56
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,680
See? The house does just fine without you.

57
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,280
Let's talk.

58
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:56,479
You drove everyone away.

59
00:03:56,879 --> 00:03:57,520
It's just the two of us now.

60
00:04:03,039 --> 00:04:04,680
Cut the martyr act.

61
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,080
I've been thinking all night,

62
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,040
and I've finally figured it out.

63
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,360
When you came to my room the other day,

64
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:19,879
you really wanted to split the money.

65
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:21,519
But as luck would have it,

66
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:23,079
you found out Xiuming resigned.

67
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,639
Ever since then, you've been up to no good.

68
00:04:25,959 --> 00:04:27,680
I still remember the look on your face when you left.

69
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:28,639
Now it all adds up.

70
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:29,800
Well?

71
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,560
Blowing the lid off this today...

72
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,120
It was all premeditated.

73
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,120
You used me as your weapon!

74
00:04:35,839 --> 00:04:37,240
Even if we don't split the money,

75
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:38,600
where do you think it'll go?

76
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,639
To the construction crew!

77
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:41,600
And even if it goes to the crew,

78
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,560
that crew belongs to the Sais!

79
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,680
And not Sai Xiuming's Sai, either.

80
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,839
It belongs to Sai Duoxi!

81
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:48,959
What's your last name? Wen Jia...

82
00:04:49,959 --> 00:04:50,920
Kid, stay out of this!

83
00:04:51,319 --> 00:04:51,639
You...

84
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:54,560
Can you please stop talking?

85
00:04:55,199 --> 00:04:55,879
You've been causing a scene all day!

86
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,120
Sister-in-law, let me help you.

87
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,639
What do you want to eat next week?

88
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,319
I'll braise some more beef for you.

89
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:18,920
Still want it spicy?

90
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,439
Go easy on the spice.

91
00:05:20,959 --> 00:05:21,639
It causes internal heat.

92
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,360
Actually, Dad's outburst...

93
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:26,199
...was bound to happen.

94
00:05:27,199 --> 00:05:28,399
Second Brother was definitely in the wrong.

95
00:05:29,279 --> 00:05:30,240
As for the beef,

96
00:05:30,839 --> 00:05:32,680
don't share it all with your classmates.

97
00:05:33,759 --> 00:05:34,720
Eat some yourself.

98
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,240
I braised it for you.

99
00:05:37,959 --> 00:05:38,720
I really think

100
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,480
there's no need to be upset over this.

101
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:42,040
Dad was mad at Second Brother,

102
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:43,160
not at you.

103
00:05:43,959 --> 00:05:44,720
Right now, Dad...

104
00:05:45,279 --> 00:05:46,720
...must still be feeling bad outside.

105
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,480
He'll be fine tomorrow.

106
00:05:49,439 --> 00:05:50,399
It's getting cold.

107
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:51,680
I'll bring you...

108
00:05:52,199 --> 00:05:53,160
...some warm clothes.

109
00:05:53,639 --> 00:05:54,839
Don't let yourself get sick.

110
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,040
You need to study hard.

111
00:05:58,319 --> 00:05:59,720
Getting into a good university...

112
00:06:00,079 --> 00:06:01,319
...is how you'll make me proud.

113
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,040
I won't let you down.

114
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,160
Tell me,

115
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,879
does this construction crew

116
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,399
still have a future?

117
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:25,439
Of course.

118
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,079
It has a future, Dad.

119
00:06:29,199 --> 00:06:29,879
Then tell me why.

120
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,120
The Olympics are already underway,

121
00:06:32,759 --> 00:06:34,279
and these past couple of years have been great.

122
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:35,920
There's more and more work.

123
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,800
Right, just a few days ago,

124
00:06:38,519 --> 00:06:39,680
Jiayin actually told me about it.

125
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:41,600
She said there's some kind of...

126
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:44,000
reg... regulation, a new rule.

127
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,399
Basically, what it means is

128
00:06:45,399 --> 00:06:46,480
a construction crew like ours

129
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:47,920
must have proper qualifications.

130
00:06:48,519 --> 00:06:49,519
Otherwise,

131
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,279
when someone like Uncle Wei lands a job,

132
00:06:51,279 --> 00:06:53,240
he can't subcontract it to a crew like ours.

133
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:55,279
We have to... have to get certified.

134
00:06:55,879 --> 00:06:56,399
Or else, they say

135
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:57,199
it's against the rules.

136
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,000
Why is your wife

137
00:07:00,519 --> 00:07:01,839
looking into this stuff anyway?

138
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,639
Isn't she doing it

139
00:07:04,279 --> 00:07:05,519
for our family's good?

140
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,000
If you ask me,

141
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:09,920
down the road,

142
00:07:10,439 --> 00:07:11,439
once I'm gone,

143
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:14,879
whether this family is still named Sai

144
00:07:15,839 --> 00:07:16,680
is hard to tell.

145
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,040
Don't say that, Dad.

146
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,279
You're still in good health.

147
00:07:23,439 --> 00:07:25,959
The wives you two brothers married are both formidable.

148
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,439
You're the eldest son.

149
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,639
You have to protect this family.

150
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,720
Don't let it fall apart.

151
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:37,600
Dad,

152
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:40,519
I'm not that sharp.

153
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:41,120
I'm slow.

154
00:07:41,279 --> 00:07:42,199
You need to...

155
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:43,879
you need to give me pointers more often.

156
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,839
Then I'll lay it all out for you today.

157
00:07:50,279 --> 00:07:52,800
Our construction crew can can't go on like this.

158
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,160
The Smart Port is a major project

159
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,800
with several phases.

160
00:07:59,279 --> 00:08:01,199
There'll be tons of work ahead.

161
00:08:01,959 --> 00:08:04,879
We can't just wait around for Uncle Wei's scraps.

162
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,160
We have to get certified ourselves

163
00:08:07,759 --> 00:08:08,480
and start a company.

164
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,360
That's how we get a piece of the pie.

165
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:12,680
About Dad...

166
00:08:15,279 --> 00:08:16,120
It's good that we got it out in the open.

167
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,759
What's done is done.

168
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,519
Your dad has no choice but to accept it.

169
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:21,879
About staying in the hotel...

170
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:23,000
does Teacher Yang know?

171
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,480
I didn't tell him.

172
00:08:25,199 --> 00:08:26,199
I didn't tell him about selling the house either.

173
00:08:27,839 --> 00:08:29,199
You keep hiding things from him.

174
00:08:29,959 --> 00:08:30,480
Is that really right?

175
00:08:30,959 --> 00:08:32,480
My dad isn't like yours.

176
00:08:33,639 --> 00:08:34,759
If he knew you sold the house,

177
00:08:34,759 --> 00:08:35,879
he'd only praise your determination.

178
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:38,039
I just worried his high expectations of you

179
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:38,879
would put too much pressure on you.

180
00:08:38,879 --> 00:08:39,679
That's why I didn't tell him.

181
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,519
You're still the one who cares about me most.

182
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:43,879
Of course.

183
00:08:44,879 --> 00:08:46,200
If I don't care about you, who will?

184
00:08:47,879 --> 00:08:48,360
Look at you,

185
00:08:48,879 --> 00:08:49,759
it's Mid-Autumn Festival,

186
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,360
and you're all alone.

187
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,039
My heart goes out to you, too.

188
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,120
Don't push your luck.

189
00:08:57,399 --> 00:08:57,799
Bye-bye.

190
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,840
What about m-me then, honey?

191
00:09:01,519 --> 00:09:02,399
You're just leaving like that?

192
00:09:03,279 --> 00:09:03,639
Honey?

193
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,240
All right, stop playing the victim.

194
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:07,919
Come on in.

195
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,759
Starting from this autumn semester,

196
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,440
the country is fully waiving

197
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:22,039
tuition and fees for urban compulsory education.

198
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:25,240
This means 28.21 million

199
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:26,600
urban students nationwide

200
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:29,519
will each save between 190

201
00:09:29,519 --> 00:09:31,360
and 350 yuan each year.

202
00:09:31,919 --> 00:09:33,559
Following the rural compulsory education

203
00:09:33,559 --> 00:09:35,240
funding security reform,

204
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,879
this major move promotes balanced development

205
00:09:38,039 --> 00:09:40,000
and advances educational equity.

206
00:09:46,759 --> 00:09:47,759
Grandpa isn't out yet,

207
00:09:47,759 --> 00:09:48,559
and you're already eating?

208
00:09:48,679 --> 00:09:49,240
Where are your manners?

209
00:10:02,399 --> 00:10:03,039
Want some porridge?

210
00:10:05,679 --> 00:10:06,960
My mom's talking to you.

211
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,879
Make sure you say my mom asked you to go.

212
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,159
Stay out of grown-ups' business.

213
00:10:24,639 --> 00:10:25,000
Big Brother.

214
00:10:29,919 --> 00:10:30,320
Dad.

215
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,399
Time to eat.

216
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,000
Dad.

217
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:45,320
Dad.

218
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:46,759
Time to eat.

219
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,559
Xiao Wu, come in.

220
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:51,919
Dad.

221
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:54,200
Sister-in-law made your favorite buns.

222
00:10:55,159 --> 00:10:56,039
Come out and have some.

223
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,120
I have no appetite.

224
00:11:08,679 --> 00:11:10,240
Eat with Dad later.

225
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,240
I won't eat here.

226
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:21,039
I wish Grandpa would stay mad for a year.

227
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,200
Why a year?

228
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,080
Then my mom could give it a rest for a year.

229
00:11:24,279 --> 00:11:24,919
By that logic,

230
00:11:24,919 --> 00:11:26,240
Grandpa should stay mad for ten years.

231
00:11:26,759 --> 00:11:27,759
Don't talk about your dad like that.

232
00:11:28,519 --> 00:11:29,759
How can you talk to your dad like that?

233
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:30,720
Mind your manners.

234
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,240
Sister-in-law was up at four to make them.

235
00:11:34,399 --> 00:11:35,519
You really won't come out to eat?

236
00:11:37,919 --> 00:11:38,360
Go on.

237
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:40,600
By the way...

238
00:11:41,279 --> 00:11:42,559
Tell your eldest brother, once he's done,

239
00:11:43,039 --> 00:11:43,759
to come to my room.

240
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:45,120
Okay.

241
00:11:58,519 --> 00:12:00,320
These are all this year's accounts.

242
00:12:00,799 --> 00:12:02,879
Take them back and study them carefully.

243
00:12:05,399 --> 00:12:05,879
Remember,

244
00:12:06,519 --> 00:12:07,200
keep them to yourself.

245
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,120
Why close the door in broad daylight?

246
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:15,039
Close the door. Close it!

247
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,279
Shut the door!

248
00:12:19,759 --> 00:12:20,360
What are you looking at?

249
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:21,519
The account books.

250
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:23,360
Dad gave me the account books.

251
00:12:28,759 --> 00:12:29,519
Still mad at me?

252
00:12:30,679 --> 00:12:31,320
Don't get cocky.

253
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,200
Dad said

254
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,279
for me to look through these two first.

255
00:12:38,039 --> 00:12:38,720
What are you doing?

256
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,159
Helping you check them. What else?

257
00:12:40,159 --> 00:12:41,000
What are you checking?

258
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Don't—don't look.

259
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,679
Dad—Dad said these books...

260
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:45,799
are only for my eyes.

261
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:51,080
Fine.

262
00:12:52,519 --> 00:12:53,039
I won't look.

263
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,039
Dad is testing you, you know.

264
00:12:58,559 --> 00:12:59,440
Of course I know that.

265
00:13:00,919 --> 00:13:01,600
Read them carefully.

266
00:13:02,039 --> 00:13:03,120
Ask me if you don't understand.

267
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:04,480
Don't try to be a hero.

268
00:13:06,399 --> 00:13:07,000
I've been doing this for years.

269
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,480
Uncle Wei.

270
00:13:28,759 --> 00:13:29,440
Xiuliang.

271
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,320
What brings you here?

272
00:13:31,559 --> 00:13:31,960
Me?

273
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:33,360
Discussing a project.

274
00:13:33,919 --> 00:13:34,320
What about you?

275
00:13:35,159 --> 00:13:36,639
I... I wanted to see Mr. Shi.

276
00:13:37,399 --> 00:13:37,879
What a coincidence.

277
00:13:40,679 --> 00:13:41,039
Thank you.

278
00:13:44,759 --> 00:13:45,200
Are you

279
00:13:45,799 --> 00:13:46,279
close with

280
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:46,919
Mr. Shi?

281
00:13:47,559 --> 00:13:48,159
Shi Yongnian?

282
00:13:49,159 --> 00:13:50,080
Known him for years.

283
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,600
Though since he took office here,

284
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,240
we haven't met yet.

285
00:13:53,039 --> 00:13:53,799
That's wonderful.

286
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,559
When I treat you to dinner later,

287
00:13:55,799 --> 00:13:56,559
we can talk in person.

288
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:58,080
I'll really need your help then.

289
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,080
Sure, sure. Another day.

290
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:01,480
Mr. Wei.

291
00:14:02,039 --> 00:14:02,320
This way, please.

292
00:14:02,679 --> 00:14:03,080
Alright.

293
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:03,960
I'll head in first.

294
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:04,240
Sure.

295
00:14:04,240 --> 00:14:05,000
We'll talk later.

296
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:05,799
Okay, go right ahead.

297
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:06,720
This way.

298
00:14:09,159 --> 00:14:09,399
Come in.

299
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,120
Mr. Wei.

300
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:14,360
Hello.

301
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:14,879
Please, have a seat.

302
00:14:19,759 --> 00:14:20,559
Allow me to introduce everyone.

303
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,000
This is

304
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,279
Attorney Zhang from our Group's Legal Department.

305
00:14:24,519 --> 00:14:25,360
Hello, hello. Nice to meet you.

306
00:14:25,559 --> 00:14:25,919
And this is

307
00:14:26,639 --> 00:14:27,039
our

308
00:14:27,039 --> 00:14:28,919
Manager Liu from Quality and Safety Oversight.

309
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:29,879
Manager Liu.

310
00:14:30,279 --> 00:14:30,840
These two

311
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,440
are colleagues from our project team.

312
00:14:33,679 --> 00:14:34,759
The reason we asked you here today

313
00:14:35,159 --> 00:14:37,639
is to address recent project issues

314
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:39,360
and have a thorough discussion.

315
00:14:39,559 --> 00:14:40,159
Of course, of course.

316
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:41,519
Mr. Wei.

317
00:14:41,759 --> 00:14:42,799
We received reports,

318
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:44,519
and have initially verified,

319
00:14:44,799 --> 00:14:45,840
that on the plot contracted

320
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,000
by Changfu Construction,

321
00:14:47,159 --> 00:14:49,039
there've been repeated incidents

322
00:14:49,039 --> 00:14:51,440
of supervisors taking bribes from your crew

323
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:52,639
to overlook material standards

324
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,559
and cut corners during construction.

325
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:55,759
Are you aware of this?

326
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,399
No, absolutely not, Manager Liu.

327
00:14:59,120 --> 00:14:59,600
Mr. Chen,

328
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,480
there's a misunderstanding here.

329
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:02,679
Well,

330
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,399
you leaders probably know

331
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:06,240
that Qingyangli Village

332
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,399
is undergoing demolition.

333
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,480
Work on a construction site

334
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,320
is so complicated.

335
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,559
So sometimes,

336
00:15:12,919 --> 00:15:14,279
offering some drinks and smokes,

337
00:15:14,279 --> 00:15:15,120
sharing a meal,

338
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,759
and building rapport

339
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,559
is just to make the work

340
00:15:18,559 --> 00:15:19,559
go a bit smoother.

341
00:15:19,759 --> 00:15:20,799
That's totally normal.

342
00:15:20,919 --> 00:15:21,320
Right?

343
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:22,240
Mr. Wei.

344
00:15:22,759 --> 00:15:24,320
On Tengyue projects,

345
00:15:24,559 --> 00:15:25,879
there's no such thing as "normal."

346
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:28,919
Any illicit benefit crosses the red line.

347
00:15:29,159 --> 00:15:30,080
We must stamp it out.

348
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:32,879
That's the prerequisite for our cooperation.

349
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:33,759
Isn't that right, Mr. Wei?

350
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,279
Yes, absolutely.

351
00:15:35,679 --> 00:15:37,039
Your explanation just now

352
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:37,879
is invalid.

353
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,639
We need a complete solution from you.

354
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:41,360
Right now.

355
00:15:43,879 --> 00:15:44,120
Wait, no...

356
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:44,960
You...

357
00:15:46,399 --> 00:15:46,679
Mr. Shi.

358
00:15:47,399 --> 00:15:47,679
Mr. Shi.

359
00:15:47,679 --> 00:15:48,120
Mr. Shi! Mr. Shi!

360
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:56,559
Everyone, out.

361
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:06,639
Brother Wei!

362
00:16:08,399 --> 00:16:09,080
Brother Wei!

363
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,840
Long time no see!

364
00:16:11,039 --> 00:16:11,799
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

365
00:16:11,799 --> 00:16:12,840
How many years has it been already?

366
00:16:13,039 --> 00:16:13,320
Yeah.

367
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,200
Still recognize me?

368
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,559
Of course, of course I do!

369
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:16,919
Come on.

370
00:16:17,559 --> 00:16:18,279
Have a seat, have a seat.

371
00:16:38,039 --> 00:16:38,480
Brother Wei.

372
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,840
You probably know I'm already in Honggang, right?

373
00:16:41,879 --> 00:16:42,879
I do, of course I know.

374
00:16:42,879 --> 00:16:43,559
How you were parachuted in

375
00:16:43,759 --> 00:16:45,840
from Tengyue's Shenzhen headquarters

376
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,799
to take charge here in Honggang.

377
00:16:47,799 --> 00:16:49,600
The news has spread all over our circle.

378
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:50,879
Then since you knew,

379
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:52,519
why didn't you come by to catch up?

380
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:54,840
Given our relationship,

381
00:16:55,279 --> 00:16:56,919
you should've met with me no matter what.

382
00:16:57,399 --> 00:16:58,919
It's been so many years, after all.

383
00:16:58,919 --> 00:16:59,759
I didn't even know

384
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,279
if you'd still remember me.

385
00:17:01,279 --> 00:17:01,679
Right?

386
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:02,279
Besides,

387
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:04,200
you're a big leader now.

388
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,720
Swamped with work day and night.

389
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,720
My small business didn't dare bother you.

390
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,960
Brother Wei, now you're just mocking me.

391
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,839
How could I ever forget you?

392
00:17:13,759 --> 00:17:14,599
What kind of bond do we have?

393
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:16,559
We've been through life and death together!

394
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,440
All right, all right.

395
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:27,279
Catching up is one thing,

396
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,720
but business is business.

397
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:31,359
As for Honggang,

398
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:33,680
the main focus is the Smart Port

399
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:35,079
and its supporting developments.

400
00:17:35,519 --> 00:17:36,559
Headquarters takes this very seriously.

401
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,160
I used to work in Honggang,

402
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,160
so they sent me over here.

403
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:41,440
My job is just to

404
00:17:42,039 --> 00:17:43,119
help clean things up

405
00:17:43,519 --> 00:17:44,240
and get things in order.

406
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:48,960
I had no idea until I dug into it,

407
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,200
and once I did...

408
00:17:51,559 --> 00:17:52,359
What can I even say?

409
00:17:53,519 --> 00:17:55,160
That plot you're in charge of...

410
00:17:55,799 --> 00:17:56,920
Why are there so many issues?

411
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,200
There are no issues.

412
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,480
Everything's normal at the site.

413
00:18:03,279 --> 00:18:03,759
Are you sure about that?

414
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:05,119
Yes, completely.

415
00:18:06,079 --> 00:18:07,240
You originally intended

416
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:09,480
to treat the old supervisor to a bath

417
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,319
so he could relax,

418
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:12,759
but things went sideways.

419
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:14,880
Then a young supervisor came along,

420
00:18:15,039 --> 00:18:16,279
and within a few days,

421
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:17,599
you managed to get him on your side too.

422
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:18,240
Am I right?

423
00:18:18,599 --> 00:18:19,519
The project supervisor

424
00:18:19,519 --> 00:18:21,119
and the crew are in bed together.

425
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,400
You call this "no issues"?

426
00:18:22,839 --> 00:18:23,480
Then what counts as an issue?

427
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:25,000
No...

428
00:18:25,559 --> 00:18:26,759
It's not that serious.

429
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,240
Look, Mr. Shi.

430
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:29,680
You just took office,

431
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,240
and the people under you

432
00:18:31,359 --> 00:18:34,039
all want to impress their new boss.

433
00:18:34,359 --> 00:18:35,720
So aren't they perhaps

434
00:18:36,079 --> 00:18:37,559
making a fuss over nothing?

435
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,799
It's not that simple.

436
00:18:39,599 --> 00:18:41,200
We've known each other for nearly 20 years.

437
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,039
Why are you still doing business like this?

438
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:45,400
Keep this up, and it'll blow up in your face.

439
00:18:46,079 --> 00:18:47,319
Given our long friendship,

440
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:49,279
there are a few things

441
00:18:49,799 --> 00:18:50,680
I must make clear upfront.

442
00:18:51,079 --> 00:18:52,079
Since they sent me here

443
00:18:52,079 --> 00:18:53,039
to take over this operation,

444
00:18:53,359 --> 00:18:54,960
I need to set a new tone

445
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,240
and lay down new rules.

446
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:57,799
From this moment on,

447
00:18:58,400 --> 00:18:59,200
under my watch,

448
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:00,960
and on Tengyue's projects,

449
00:19:01,359 --> 00:19:03,240
things like this can never happen again.

450
00:19:03,839 --> 00:19:05,119
If it happens one more time,

451
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:06,720
Brother Wei,

452
00:19:07,759 --> 00:19:08,640
don't blame me

453
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:10,240
for not warning you beforehand.

454
00:19:11,039 --> 00:19:11,440
Got it?

455
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:16,119
Well...

456
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,480
I... I understand, Mr. Shi.

457
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:19,599
Rest assured,

458
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,920
I'll rectify everything thoroughly,

459
00:19:22,079 --> 00:19:25,000
strictly complying with your and Tengyue's rules.

460
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:34,039
That's what I like to hear, Brother Wei.

461
00:19:35,759 --> 00:19:36,279
Brother Wei,

462
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,279
I really wanted

463
00:19:38,279 --> 00:19:40,119
to sit down and catch up with you properly,

464
00:19:40,519 --> 00:19:41,319
but I have a meeting

465
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:41,920
and need to get going.

466
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:43,240
I'll treat you to tea another day.

467
00:19:43,319 --> 00:19:43,920
Sure, of course. Go ahead.

468
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:44,559
Tea is on me next time,

469
00:19:44,559 --> 00:19:45,240
and we'll have a good talk.

470
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:45,799
Go attend to your work.

471
00:19:45,799 --> 00:19:46,200
Sounds good?

472
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:46,920
Sounds great.

473
00:19:47,279 --> 00:19:48,519
It was really good seeing you.

474
00:19:49,079 --> 00:19:49,480
Likewise, likewise.

475
00:19:49,759 --> 00:19:50,200
Brother Wei.

476
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:50,759
Take care.

477
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,079
Uncle Wei.

478
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:06,160
It's over.

479
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,279
Look, I... I have something to handle at home.

480
00:20:08,559 --> 00:20:09,480
Let's talk another day.

481
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:35,440
Mr. Sai.

482
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:37,920
Is Mr. Shi available?

483
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,359
Mr. Shi is still in a meeting.

484
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:40,759
If it's something urgent,

485
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:41,759
you can tell me directly.

486
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,480
I just need a quick word with Mr. Shi.

487
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:46,839
Five minutes is all I need.

488
00:20:47,319 --> 00:20:48,480
I called several times to make an appointment,

489
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:49,039
but couldn't get one.

490
00:20:51,319 --> 00:20:52,519
Why don't you head back for now?

491
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:53,799
We can reschedule for another day.

492
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:00,599
Not even five minutes?

493
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:08,279
That's all right.

494
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:09,559
I'll wait.

495
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:12,680
Okay.

496
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:13,599
Please wait a moment.

497
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:25,599
Hello, President Shi.

498
00:21:26,519 --> 00:21:28,440
Section Chief Sai from the Port Authority is still waiting.

499
00:21:29,599 --> 00:21:29,880
Okay.

500
00:21:32,559 --> 00:21:32,880
This way.

501
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:47,000
Section Chief Sai, please.

502
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:04,400
I'm so sorry,

503
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:05,640
to keep you waiting.

504
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,680
What an honor to have you here, Section Chief Sai.

505
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:08,559
What brings you by?

506
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:10,839
I didn't wait long.

507
00:22:15,039 --> 00:22:15,839
Just outside,

508
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:17,200
I ran into Uncle Wei.

509
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:18,799
Wei Changfu from Changfu Construction.

510
00:22:20,119 --> 00:22:21,319
Didn't expect such a coincidence.

511
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:24,119
Actually, Uncle Wei and I are pretty close.

512
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:25,960
He watched me grow up.

513
00:22:37,519 --> 00:22:38,279
How's your dad?

514
00:22:39,319 --> 00:22:39,920
How's his health?

515
00:22:42,359 --> 00:22:43,400
You know my dad, Mr. Shi?

516
00:22:45,079 --> 00:22:45,440
Not really.

517
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:48,519
I spent some time in Honggang back then.

518
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:52,440
Let's just say I know of him.

519
00:22:56,799 --> 00:22:57,079
Have a seat.

520
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:08,119
Starting your own business,

521
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:09,880
opening a law firm...

522
00:23:10,839 --> 00:23:11,359
That's great.

523
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,079
But this iron rice bowl of yours,

524
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:14,480
throwing it away just like that?

525
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:16,400
Will your dad actually agree to this?

526
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:18,519
I make my own decisions about my life.

527
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,000
Yet as far as I know,

528
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,440
back then, your dad

529
00:23:21,599 --> 00:23:23,440
sold everything he had to put you through college,

530
00:23:23,759 --> 00:23:26,079
hoping that one day you'd wear the government uniform

531
00:23:26,279 --> 00:23:27,240
and live on a government paycheck.

532
00:23:27,799 --> 00:23:28,319
Am I right?

533
00:23:29,039 --> 00:23:29,880
Besides,

534
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,559
you've been working hard for over a decade,

535
00:23:31,839 --> 00:23:33,799
finally made it to section-level cadre,

536
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:35,799
and now you're giving it up just like that?

537
00:23:36,079 --> 00:23:37,440
Can you really get past your dad on this?

538
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:46,640
Let's not dwell on that. Let's move on.

539
00:23:47,519 --> 00:23:48,519
Come on, tell me.

540
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:49,720
Starting a law firm—

541
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:51,440
how much do you plan to make?

542
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:52,559
Just casual talk.

543
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:55,559
Mr. Shi, it's not about the money.

544
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:56,440
Really?

545
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,640
I know your type.

546
00:23:59,039 --> 00:24:00,519
You must have calculated every move.

547
00:24:01,279 --> 00:24:01,920
And another thing,

548
00:24:02,160 --> 00:24:02,799
let me ask you:

549
00:24:02,799 --> 00:24:03,920
what makes you think

550
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:05,119
you'd have an opportunity with me?

551
00:24:10,160 --> 00:24:10,519
Mr. Shi,

552
00:24:11,759 --> 00:24:13,319
the Smart Port is Honggang's

553
00:24:13,319 --> 00:24:15,720
core project for the next five to ten years.

554
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:17,000
Tengyue is fully capable.

555
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:18,079
That's a fact,

556
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:19,240
and everyone knows it.

557
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:21,119
But you're an outsider firm after all.

558
00:24:21,519 --> 00:24:22,880
To do business in a new place,

559
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:24,240
first comes connections,

560
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:25,680
followed by laws and regulations.

561
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:27,000
Since we hit it off,

562
00:24:27,279 --> 00:24:28,400
I can let you in on something.

563
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:30,279
In all of Honggang,

564
00:24:31,759 --> 00:24:32,880
the most influential lawyers

565
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:35,359
are all students of my father-in-law, Yang Guangqi.

566
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,880
And my mother-in-law, Su Yuru,

567
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:37,599
she's with the Design and Planning Institute...

568
00:24:37,599 --> 00:24:38,440
All right, all right.

569
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:39,400
That's enough. I get the point.

570
00:24:39,839 --> 00:24:40,319
Section Chief Sai,

571
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:42,759
for a conglomerate as large as mine,

572
00:24:43,359 --> 00:24:45,279
you must know we have our own legal department.

573
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:45,960
I know that.

574
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:49,559
But isn't Legal managed by group headquarters?

575
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:52,319
Headquarters might not understand Honggang.

576
00:24:52,599 --> 00:24:53,640
You came here

577
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:54,960
to make big moves.

578
00:24:55,559 --> 00:24:57,039
You still need locals

579
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:58,559
to deal with locals.

580
00:24:59,400 --> 00:24:59,920
Keep going.

581
00:25:00,279 --> 00:25:02,119
At the bidding conference that day,

582
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:03,480
why did you leave so abruptly?

583
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:04,279
You haven't forgotten, have you?

584
00:25:04,599 --> 00:25:05,359
That's simple.

585
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:07,519
I knew I couldn't beat them,

586
00:25:07,759 --> 00:25:08,960
but I didn't want them to win either.

587
00:25:09,319 --> 00:25:09,920
So I walked out.

588
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:11,720
Then what did we talk about in the restroom?

589
00:25:11,839 --> 00:25:12,880
Let me refresh your memory.

590
00:25:18,319 --> 00:25:18,839
Sai Xiuliang,

591
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,079
if you truly believe in your heart

592
00:25:22,079 --> 00:25:23,000
that you did me a favor,

593
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:24,599
then you're dead wrong.

594
00:25:24,599 --> 00:25:25,519
Don't forget,

595
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,799
back when you talked to me,

596
00:25:26,799 --> 00:25:28,240
you hadn't even resigned from the Port Authority.

597
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:29,599
What kind of violation that is,

598
00:25:29,599 --> 00:25:30,480
you should know very well.

599
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:31,680
Even taking a step back,

600
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:32,599
let's just assume:

601
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:33,839
could someone

602
00:25:34,279 --> 00:25:35,400
at the Port Authority already know

603
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:36,559
what you discussed with me?

604
00:25:36,799 --> 00:25:38,240
Could it be that in the restroom that day,

605
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:39,319
besides you and me,

606
00:25:39,319 --> 00:25:40,240
there was someone else?

607
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:41,079
What if one day,

608
00:25:41,079 --> 00:25:42,759
someone barges into my office with a recording,

609
00:25:42,759 --> 00:25:44,079
sits right where you're sitting,

610
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:46,039
and threatens me?

611
00:26:09,839 --> 00:26:10,680
I've gotta take two more pills.

612
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:11,680
Can't be careless.

613
00:26:16,960 --> 00:26:18,119
What's up, Old Wei?

614
00:26:18,240 --> 00:26:19,079
What's the matter with you?

615
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:20,079
Look, Duoxi,

616
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:23,000
can't you do your job properly?

617
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:24,759
What didn't I do properly?

618
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:26,640
What happened with that old supervisor?

619
00:26:27,119 --> 00:26:28,559
How did he end up at the police station?

620
00:26:29,559 --> 00:26:30,799
That's all in the past.

621
00:26:31,039 --> 00:26:32,240
He's already left.

622
00:26:33,119 --> 00:26:34,599
That jerk was completely out of line.

623
00:26:34,880 --> 00:26:35,640
On the job site—

624
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:36,160
Alright, alright, alright.

625
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,480
Don't—don't bring that up.

626
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:38,680
The problem right now is,

627
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:39,799
they've come asking about it.

628
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:41,079
Who's asking?

629
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:50,079
He looks familiar.

630
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:53,119
Isn't that Huzi?

631
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:58,880
He's moved up in the world now.

632
00:26:59,160 --> 00:27:00,359
You have to call him Mr. Shi.

633
00:27:00,519 --> 00:27:01,680
Tengyue Real Estate,

634
00:27:01,960 --> 00:27:02,799
here in Honggang—

635
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:04,400
he's their newly appointed head.

636
00:27:04,559 --> 00:27:06,119
Our main client, you know?

637
00:27:08,039 --> 00:27:09,680
Back when we took him in on the site,

638
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:10,799
aside from brute strength,

639
00:27:10,799 --> 00:27:11,920
he didn't know how to do squat, right?

640
00:27:12,279 --> 00:27:12,880
Look at him now.

641
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:13,920
He's turned himself

642
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,720
into a real estate tycoon.

643
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:17,319
When did he come back?

644
00:27:17,799 --> 00:27:18,759
He's been back for a while.

645
00:27:18,759 --> 00:27:19,559
I didn't tell you guys

646
00:27:19,559 --> 00:27:20,440
so you wouldn't overthink it.

647
00:27:21,079 --> 00:27:21,839
Anyway, as for us,

648
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:23,279
we just do our work.

649
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:25,039
He didn't ask if you two were around,

650
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:26,440
so I didn't bring it up.

651
00:27:27,519 --> 00:27:28,720
He didn't ask about us?

652
00:27:30,839 --> 00:27:31,759
Why would he ask about you two?

653
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:32,720
Ask what?

654
00:27:35,319 --> 00:27:36,039
Great, now look.

655
00:27:36,640 --> 00:27:37,680
With the fuss over the old supervisor,

656
00:27:37,680 --> 00:27:38,440
it's all out in the open.

657
00:27:38,799 --> 00:27:39,799
Us three old faces...

658
00:27:40,319 --> 00:27:41,519
Who knows if he'll even acknowledge us.

659
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:46,680
After all these years...

660
00:27:47,480 --> 00:27:47,759
Why...

661
00:27:48,119 --> 00:27:49,799
why did he suddenly come back?

662
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:53,960
Old Fang,

663
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:55,359
tell me again:

664
00:27:55,920 --> 00:27:57,880
how much was that sand and gravel per ton?

665
00:27:58,839 --> 00:27:59,519
Fifty yuan.

666
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:02,000
What do you think?

667
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:03,960
Old Fang,

668
00:28:04,359 --> 00:28:06,839
how much is transit loss for sand and gravel normally?

669
00:28:06,839 --> 00:28:07,640
Tell us about it.

670
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:09,880
That's around two percent.

671
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:11,680
What loss?

672
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,480
Hauling it dozens of kilometers to our site,

673
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:17,079
the truck bumps around the whole way.

674
00:28:17,079 --> 00:28:19,079
It's bound to spill and leak some.

675
00:28:19,319 --> 00:28:20,759
A truck isn't a magic pot of gold.

676
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,720
Right, it's not going to multiply as it bumps.

677
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:24,920
What about Pockmark Wang?

678
00:28:25,440 --> 00:28:25,799
Did he...

679
00:28:26,359 --> 00:28:27,839
over all these years,

680
00:28:27,839 --> 00:28:28,519
when we settled up with him,

681
00:28:28,519 --> 00:28:29,480
did he ever issue us invoices?

682
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:30,759
What invoice?

683
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:32,160
We squeezed the price down so low.

684
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:33,319
The main thing was it was cheap,

685
00:28:33,319 --> 00:28:33,960
you know?

686
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:34,640
All right, fine.

687
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:35,680
Hey, Heizi.

688
00:28:36,119 --> 00:28:37,000
That excavator of yours,

689
00:28:37,559 --> 00:28:38,680
how much fuel does it take?

690
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:39,960
I honestly forgot. Why?

691
00:28:40,039 --> 00:28:40,799
You forgot? You should still know

692
00:28:40,799 --> 00:28:42,200
how much the average daily fuel cost is, right?

693
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:43,839
Bro, you really can't calculate an average.

694
00:28:44,119 --> 00:28:45,440
Sometimes the excavator sits idle for days,

695
00:28:45,440 --> 00:28:46,440
and sometimes it runs days on end without a break.

696
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:48,000
How can you average that daily?

697
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,359
Uncle Duoxi told me,

698
00:28:49,359 --> 00:28:50,440
each time we refuel,

699
00:28:50,759 --> 00:28:52,920
to mark the amount in chalk inside the fuel cap.

700
00:28:53,319 --> 00:28:54,519
He checks it himself every day,

701
00:28:54,599 --> 00:28:56,000
so I never bothered memorizing it.

702
00:28:57,319 --> 00:28:58,599
What you reported to Qingyou,

703
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:00,240
was it what was written in chalk?

704
00:29:00,319 --> 00:29:01,240
Yeah, that exact number.

705
00:29:03,359 --> 00:29:06,519
There's no way those two numbers wouldn't match.

706
00:29:07,319 --> 00:29:07,839
All right, you two.

707
00:29:07,960 --> 00:29:08,319
Back to work.

708
00:29:15,559 --> 00:29:16,160
Brother Mingming,

709
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,599
the hardest accounts in the world to keep

710
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:20,160
are the construction site books.

711
00:29:20,599 --> 00:29:22,240
Materials, shipping,

712
00:29:22,319 --> 00:29:23,599
labor, wear and tear,

713
00:29:24,039 --> 00:29:25,160
daily coordination and greasing wheels...

714
00:29:25,559 --> 00:29:26,599
all of that takes money, doesn't it?

715
00:29:27,039 --> 00:29:28,480
Contract flow, invoice flow,

716
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:29,559
cargo flow, and cash flow—

717
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:30,319
a four-way match.

718
00:29:30,319 --> 00:29:30,920
Not a single one can be missing.

719
00:29:31,079 --> 00:29:31,920
They have to correspond strictly.

720
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:32,480
Did you know that?

721
00:29:33,079 --> 00:29:33,839
And there are so many expenses...

722
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:35,319
If we don't pad them into fuel costs,

723
00:29:35,720 --> 00:29:36,400
or pad them in here,

724
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,000
or pad them in there,

725
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:38,079
tell me, with all these expenses,

726
00:29:38,079 --> 00:29:38,640
what am I supposed to do?

727
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:40,079
Are you going to pay, or should I?

728
00:29:40,839 --> 00:29:41,640
I'm asking for your advice.

729
00:29:42,480 --> 00:29:43,039
Let me ask you:

730
00:29:43,039 --> 00:29:44,640
However you tell me to book it, I will.

731
00:29:47,319 --> 00:29:48,640
Speak up! Tell me!

732
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:49,799
Tell me, and I'll leave right now!

733
00:29:49,799 --> 00:29:50,720
Wouldn't that settle it?

734
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:51,839
All day long,

735
00:29:51,839 --> 00:29:53,079
knowing nothing, you just keep pestering me,

736
00:29:53,279 --> 00:29:54,319
acting like you actually know what you're doing!

737
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:55,759
I've really had it with you. I really have.

738
00:29:59,319 --> 00:30:00,319
Sai Duoxi.

739
00:30:02,279 --> 00:30:03,200
Fine. Thanks. Thanks a lot.

740
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:23,559
That's impossible.

741
00:30:23,799 --> 00:30:26,319
How could it suddenly... suddenly be late-stage?

742
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:29,160
The MRI suggested this possibility at the time.

743
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:30,839
That's why we did the biopsy.

744
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:31,359
Look here.

745
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:32,680
This pathology report...

746
00:30:33,039 --> 00:30:34,160
...states it very clearly.

747
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:36,319
No, but with all these tests you ran,

748
00:30:36,319 --> 00:30:37,319
back and forth,

749
00:30:38,279 --> 00:30:39,279
the results were all different.

750
00:30:39,279 --> 00:30:40,799
So who... who am I supposed to believe?

751
00:30:40,920 --> 00:30:41,880
A definitive diagnosis...

752
00:30:42,440 --> 00:30:44,400
...is based on the biopsy.

753
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:46,519
That's all you need to keep in mind.

754
00:30:46,680 --> 00:30:47,680
No, but...

755
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:51,680
This...

756
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:52,279
Does this mean...

757
00:30:52,799 --> 00:30:53,720
...it's con... confirmed?

758
00:30:58,799 --> 00:30:59,160
Cancer?

759
00:31:00,599 --> 00:31:01,160
Late-stage?

760
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:08,000
Just... just how late is it?

761
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,519
Based on what we see right now,

762
00:31:09,599 --> 00:31:10,960
it's Stage T3.

763
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:12,400
That means...

764
00:31:12,559 --> 00:31:13,200
...early Stage III.

765
00:31:13,359 --> 00:31:14,359
Locally advanced.

766
00:31:14,559 --> 00:31:15,680
Simply put,

767
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:17,160
the cancer cells...

768
00:31:17,359 --> 00:31:18,480
...have already broken out.

769
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:19,960
Looking at the imaging scans,

770
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:21,559
there's a risk of metastasis.

771
00:31:22,519 --> 00:31:24,200
So considering your situation,

772
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:25,519
we recommend that you...

773
00:31:25,920 --> 00:31:26,599
...get admitted right away...

774
00:31:27,039 --> 00:31:28,640
...for a comprehensive examination.

775
00:31:29,079 --> 00:31:29,599
Then,

776
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:30,920
we can work out a treatment plan.

777
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:31,599
As for you,

778
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:32,640
once you get home,

779
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:34,319
discuss this with your family right away.

780
00:31:34,799 --> 00:31:36,279
If you're getting admitted, don't wait.

781
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:37,680
It can't be delayed any longer.

782
00:32:02,880 --> 00:32:03,319
Uncle,

783
00:32:03,599 --> 00:32:06,039
did you have Brother Mingming audit my accounts again?

784
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:08,039
Didn't we already agree on this?

785
00:32:08,039 --> 00:32:10,119
This was just between the two of us!

786
00:32:10,920 --> 00:32:12,279
And then he barges onto the job site,

787
00:32:12,279 --> 00:32:14,000
throwing his weight around to audit my accounts!

788
00:32:14,759 --> 00:32:16,880
I saved everyone money on the job,

789
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:18,480
so why isn't he mentioning that at all?!

790
00:32:18,759 --> 00:32:20,559
He practically accused me of embezzling!

791
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:21,799
I'm telling you, Uncle,

792
00:32:21,799 --> 00:32:23,240
if this is how it's going to be,

793
00:32:23,240 --> 00:32:24,359
I don't even want to do this anymore.

794
00:32:24,799 --> 00:32:26,000
Just let me quit!

795
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:27,519
After all my devotion,

796
00:32:27,519 --> 00:32:29,200
all the years I've given to this family,

797
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:30,559
look at everything I've done!

798
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,160
From what we can see,

799
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:46,839
it's Stage T3.

800
00:32:47,400 --> 00:32:48,599
Judging from the scans,

801
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:50,200
there's a risk of metastasis.

802
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:52,039
We suggest that you

803
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,079
get admitted right away

804
00:32:53,559 --> 00:32:55,119
for a comprehensive checkup.

805
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:56,119
After that,

806
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:57,440
we'll figure out a treatment plan.

807
00:32:57,720 --> 00:32:58,079
When you

808
00:32:58,440 --> 00:32:59,160
get back home,

809
00:32:59,480 --> 00:33:00,799
discuss it with your family right away.

810
00:33:01,319 --> 00:33:02,799
If you're getting admitted, don't delay.

811
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:04,160
It can't wait any longer.

812
00:33:06,640 --> 00:33:07,559
You could take a look at this one.

813
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:08,640
If you wear this,

814
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:10,039
it'll really flatter your figure.

815
00:33:10,240 --> 00:33:11,079
This one...

816
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:11,880
how much is it?

817
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:12,839
Eight thousand.

818
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:13,640
Okay.

819
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:14,880
Could you get me...

820
00:33:15,759 --> 00:33:16,440
a few sizes up?

821
00:33:16,799 --> 00:33:17,240
A bigger one.

822
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:18,200
Sure thing.

823
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:19,039
Just a moment.

824
00:33:35,599 --> 00:33:36,799
A new haircut.

825
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:38,960
A new suit.

826
00:33:41,079 --> 00:33:43,839
Sai Duoxi considers himself a respectable man.

827
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:46,279
Kids?

828
00:33:46,759 --> 00:33:47,279
Plenty.

829
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:49,599
Plenty of money, too.

830
00:33:51,680 --> 00:33:52,839
The sun is shining bright.

831
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:56,119
What a wonderful day.

832
00:33:58,599 --> 00:34:00,160
The only catch

833
00:34:00,920 --> 00:34:01,680
is this illness.

834
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,079
And it's pretty deadly.

835
00:34:06,759 --> 00:34:07,960
And this deadly secret,

836
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:11,039
he can't let anyone find out.

837
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:13,800
At least,

838
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:16,159
not right now.

839
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:25,719
How much longer does he have?

840
00:34:26,519 --> 00:34:27,400
Surgery first,

841
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,599
followed by systemic treatment.

842
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:32,039
Dad's always been in pretty good shape.

843
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:32,760
Seven years,

844
00:34:33,679 --> 00:34:36,000
eight, ten, or even longer is possible.

845
00:34:36,159 --> 00:34:37,360
But the pressing matter right now

846
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,840
is that we really need to make a decision.

847
00:34:49,079 --> 00:34:49,880
What if he doesn't have surgery?

848
00:34:52,920 --> 00:34:53,599
Six months to a year.

849
00:34:55,800 --> 00:34:56,239
How long?

850
00:34:57,159 --> 00:34:58,199
So you have to trust me.

851
00:34:58,920 --> 00:35:00,480
We have to be upfront with him.

852
00:35:01,880 --> 00:35:02,800
We really can't keep it from him.

853
00:35:06,519 --> 00:35:07,719
I'm a professional doctor.

854
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,880
I've seen every kind of patient at the hospital.

855
00:35:11,199 --> 00:35:12,960
Some change drastically and push loved ones away,

856
00:35:13,519 --> 00:35:15,119
some only think about the feelings of others

857
00:35:15,119 --> 00:35:16,559
with no regard for their own lives,

858
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:18,320
and some pray to gods and spirits,

859
00:35:18,559 --> 00:35:19,800
putting their faith in superstition

860
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:21,000
instead of trusting us doctors.

861
00:35:21,280 --> 00:35:22,199
I've seen it all.

862
00:35:22,719 --> 00:35:23,679
But with something this serious,

863
00:35:24,519 --> 00:35:26,079
no family could handle it easily.

864
00:35:26,880 --> 00:35:27,559
With an illness this severe,

865
00:35:28,119 --> 00:35:30,079
you can't let him shoulder it alone.

866
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:32,119
Most importantly,

867
00:35:32,559 --> 00:35:34,880
we can't miss the best window for treatment.

868
00:35:35,239 --> 00:35:37,039
Otherwise, it'll be too late for regrets.

869
00:35:50,800 --> 00:35:52,559
Just tell me, are you an idiot?

870
00:35:52,559 --> 00:35:53,159
Seriously, what is wrong with you?

871
00:35:53,400 --> 00:35:54,440
Who says I'm an idiot?

872
00:35:54,760 --> 00:35:55,639
There's an issue with the two ledgers.

873
00:35:55,639 --> 00:35:56,360
Shouldn't I talk to him about it?

874
00:35:56,719 --> 00:35:57,199
And shouldn't I

875
00:35:57,199 --> 00:35:57,920
ask him to explain it to me?

876
00:35:57,920 --> 00:35:58,800
What is there for him to explain?

877
00:35:58,960 --> 00:35:59,920
If he couldn't explain it,

878
00:36:00,039 --> 00:36:01,000
would he dare put it on the books?

879
00:36:01,239 --> 00:36:02,320
He explained it, and that was that.

880
00:36:02,519 --> 00:36:03,599
I didn't even say anything bad.

881
00:36:03,599 --> 00:36:05,159
What more could you say?

882
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:06,639
You couldn't understand the ledgers,

883
00:36:06,639 --> 00:36:07,480
and when I offered to help,

884
00:36:07,480 --> 00:36:08,079
you wouldn't let me.

885
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:09,559
Then you confronted him,

886
00:36:09,960 --> 00:36:11,320
and tipped him off! Don't you see?

887
00:36:12,519 --> 00:36:14,239
Tipped him off? How did I tip him off?

888
00:36:14,239 --> 00:36:15,880
If there's a problem, shouldn't I handle it?

889
00:36:16,159 --> 00:36:16,800
Then tell me,

890
00:36:17,159 --> 00:36:18,719
why did Dad give me the ledgers?

891
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:20,920
Wasn't it for me to find problems?

892
00:36:20,920 --> 00:36:21,760
If I couldn't find any,

893
00:36:21,760 --> 00:36:22,880
that's when I'd be an idiot!

894
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:23,480
Xiuming.

895
00:36:24,400 --> 00:36:24,960
Come down here for a second.

896
00:36:28,280 --> 00:36:28,639
Coming!

897
00:36:31,079 --> 00:36:31,559
What is it?

898
00:36:32,119 --> 00:36:32,639
Apologize.

899
00:36:33,039 --> 00:36:33,880
Apologize as soon as you walk in.

900
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:34,559
Apologize for what?

901
00:36:34,880 --> 00:36:35,639
What did I do wrong?

902
00:36:35,639 --> 00:36:35,920
You...

903
00:36:36,519 --> 00:36:37,519
This is ridiculous.

904
00:36:37,719 --> 00:36:38,400
All day long,

905
00:36:38,400 --> 00:36:39,239
both at home and outside,

906
00:36:39,239 --> 00:36:40,199
you're the only one who thinks I'm stupid.

907
00:36:43,880 --> 00:36:44,360
Stop looking.

908
00:36:45,679 --> 00:36:46,360
Just apologize.

909
00:36:57,199 --> 00:36:57,519
Dad.

910
00:37:02,199 --> 00:37:02,719
You wanted to see me?

911
00:37:09,320 --> 00:37:09,639
Dad...

912
00:37:09,960 --> 00:37:10,960
Those ledgers you gave me,

913
00:37:11,760 --> 00:37:12,480
I went through them.

914
00:37:13,039 --> 00:37:13,599
There's a problem.

915
00:37:14,280 --> 00:37:15,480
Pretty shady business, too.

916
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:17,239
Yang Qingyou

917
00:37:18,599 --> 00:37:19,320
has been pocketing money.

918
00:37:19,599 --> 00:37:21,159
At least five or six entries a month.

919
00:37:25,519 --> 00:37:26,079
And then?

920
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:27,639
So I went to see him today.

921
00:37:28,599 --> 00:37:29,079
Don't worry,

922
00:37:29,559 --> 00:37:30,719
I didn't take the ledgers with me.

923
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:32,119
I kept it all in my head,

924
00:37:32,119 --> 00:37:33,719
and went over every entry with him.

925
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:34,599
Dad, let me tell you,

926
00:37:34,800 --> 00:37:35,519
with Yang Qingyou,

927
00:37:35,719 --> 00:37:37,239
you've got to keep him in line once in a while.

928
00:37:37,719 --> 00:37:38,239
Let him know

929
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:39,400
that the two of us

930
00:37:39,679 --> 00:37:41,559
know those site accounts

931
00:37:41,559 --> 00:37:42,440
inside and out.

932
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:44,239
I didn't lose my temper this time.

933
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:46,039
I just let him know

934
00:37:46,719 --> 00:37:47,519
that I've got leverage on him.

935
00:37:48,199 --> 00:37:48,880
I didn't expose him.

936
00:37:52,760 --> 00:37:53,480
What's wrong, Dad?

937
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:57,880
Are you feeling unwell?

938
00:37:58,559 --> 00:37:58,920
Let me

939
00:37:59,239 --> 00:37:59,760
take your blood pressure.

940
00:38:00,559 --> 00:38:01,000
Son.

941
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:03,760
Go.

942
00:38:05,119 --> 00:38:06,199
Bring all the ledgers down.

943
00:38:09,199 --> 00:38:09,920
Go on!

944
00:38:22,559 --> 00:38:23,199
Did he chew you out?

945
00:38:25,559 --> 00:38:26,119
He didn't scold me.

946
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:28,679
Why would he scold me?

947
00:38:30,719 --> 00:38:31,599
Why bring out the ledger?

948
00:38:39,679 --> 00:38:41,000
See where I marked in red?

949
00:38:42,880 --> 00:38:45,320
That's all money spent on entertaining clients.

950
00:38:46,679 --> 00:38:47,360
Second,

951
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:49,360
the ones underlined in blue.

952
00:38:49,920 --> 00:38:50,480
This is...

953
00:38:50,920 --> 00:38:51,840
money Qingyou

954
00:38:52,519 --> 00:38:54,159
scraped together for us.

955
00:38:54,880 --> 00:38:55,679
Third,

956
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:56,599
do you see this?

957
00:38:57,079 --> 00:38:57,960
The ones marked in pencil.

958
00:38:58,159 --> 00:38:59,679
He skimmed fifty here,

959
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:01,440
a hundred there.

960
00:39:02,960 --> 00:39:04,119
That's his little slush fund.

961
00:39:04,599 --> 00:39:05,800
That's a lot of money, Dad.

962
00:39:06,199 --> 00:39:07,280
He's way too slick.

963
00:39:07,360 --> 00:39:08,599
You know the saying, right?

964
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:10,239
"Water that's too clear has no fish."

965
00:39:10,599 --> 00:39:12,119
As long as it's under thirty thousand,

966
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:14,760
consider it a bonus from me.

967
00:39:15,639 --> 00:39:16,719
Looking at the bottom line,

968
00:39:17,079 --> 00:39:18,599
we won't come out behind.

969
00:39:18,960 --> 00:39:20,400
The last time Sai Duoxi

970
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:22,360
guided his eldest son like this

971
00:39:23,679 --> 00:39:25,000
was twenty years ago,

972
00:39:25,760 --> 00:39:27,239
when he left town for a day

973
00:39:28,239 --> 00:39:30,000
and told Xiuming to look after the house.

974
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:32,320
Yet this time,

975
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:36,559
Sai Duoxi sensed he was going far away.

976
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:40,400
If he could never come back,

977
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:42,559
this family

978
00:39:43,559 --> 00:39:45,840
would still fall on his eldest to look after.

979
00:39:56,159 --> 00:39:56,480
Hello?

980
00:39:57,159 --> 00:39:57,719
Supervisor Wang,

981
00:39:58,199 --> 00:39:58,920
are you out yet?

982
00:39:59,320 --> 00:39:59,920
You okay?

983
00:40:00,239 --> 00:40:00,840
Qingyou,

984
00:40:02,519 --> 00:40:05,360
I just can't take this lying down.

985
00:40:06,079 --> 00:40:06,719
Don't forget,

986
00:40:07,039 --> 00:40:07,960
the trap he set

987
00:40:08,159 --> 00:40:09,719
was meant to screw us both over.

988
00:40:10,039 --> 00:40:11,960
He's never trusted you.

989
00:40:12,239 --> 00:40:13,079
Didn't they

990
00:40:13,320 --> 00:40:14,840
even audit your books today?

991
00:40:15,079 --> 00:40:16,280
Isn't it time

992
00:40:16,519 --> 00:40:19,000
the Sais learned a lesson?

993
00:40:19,639 --> 00:40:20,360
What are you going to do?

994
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:22,880
You're on duty tonight, right?

995
00:40:23,440 --> 00:40:24,599
I'm coming over to have a chat.

996
00:40:46,599 --> 00:40:47,039
Qingyou.

997
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:49,320
Didn't you say

998
00:40:49,519 --> 00:40:50,679
we were meeting to talk?

999
00:40:50,679 --> 00:40:52,760
What's with bringing these two big trucks?

1000
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,960
I brought two truckloads of sea sand

1001
00:40:55,199 --> 00:40:56,480
to mix into the sand on site.

1002
00:40:56,719 --> 00:40:57,119
What?

1003
00:40:58,079 --> 00:40:58,639
Sea sand?

1004
00:40:58,960 --> 00:41:00,320
Have you learned nothing all these years?

1005
00:41:00,679 --> 00:41:02,159
Don't you know if you mix in sea sand,

1006
00:41:02,159 --> 00:41:03,079
the building will collapse?

1007
00:41:03,239 --> 00:41:03,920
That's a crime!

1008
00:41:04,199 --> 00:41:04,840
Don't worry.

1009
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:05,920
Right after it's unloaded,

1010
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:07,679
I'll call the tip line.

1011
00:41:08,159 --> 00:41:09,840
An inspection team will be here tomorrow.

1012
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:12,639
I'll teach the Sai family a lesson.

1013
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:13,639
Don't worry, it'll be fine.

1014
00:41:14,039 --> 00:41:15,719
I'll show him what it feels like to get reported.

1015
00:41:15,960 --> 00:41:16,400
Come on, over here.

1016
00:41:16,400 --> 00:41:17,760
Are these guys reliable?

1017
00:41:58,719 --> 00:42:00,199
I'm here.

1018
00:42:08,239 --> 00:42:08,840
Slow down, slow down.

1019
00:42:15,039 --> 00:42:15,559
What are you doing?

1020
00:42:17,880 --> 00:42:18,440
I...

1021
00:42:21,280 --> 00:42:22,559
There's something I need to tell you.

1022
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:25,239
Let's talk later.

1023
00:42:36,440 --> 00:42:37,599
Hey, Jin!

1024
00:42:37,760 --> 00:42:38,079
No, no.

1025
00:42:38,320 --> 00:42:39,400
Are you gonna behave?

1026
00:42:39,480 --> 00:42:39,960
Qianjin, Qianjin!

1027
00:42:40,320 --> 00:42:40,679
One.

1028
00:42:42,079 --> 00:42:42,679
Two.

1029
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:47,880
Dad?

1030
00:42:49,519 --> 00:42:50,239
Where's Jingran?

1031
00:42:50,239 --> 00:42:51,239
Why hasn't he called me?

1032
00:42:51,239 --> 00:42:51,719
What do you want with him?

1033
00:42:51,719 --> 00:42:52,400
Dad, Dad, Dad...

1034
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:53,400
I need to ask him something.

1035
00:42:53,480 --> 00:42:53,800
For me?

1036
00:42:53,800 --> 00:42:54,840
Put him on the phone.

1037
00:42:56,119 --> 00:42:56,440
Dad.

1038
00:42:57,320 --> 00:42:57,880
It's me, Jingran.

1039
00:42:58,519 --> 00:42:58,760
Dad.

1040
00:42:59,039 --> 00:42:59,400
Go ahead.

1041
00:43:00,039 --> 00:43:01,960
Well, in our construction crew,

1042
00:43:01,960 --> 00:43:03,360
there's a fitter.

1043
00:43:04,199 --> 00:43:05,400
He's got this...

1044
00:43:07,079 --> 00:43:08,480
prostate...

1045
00:43:09,559 --> 00:43:09,920
cancer.

1046
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:20,280
Dad,

1047
00:43:20,760 --> 00:43:21,400
listen to me.

1048
00:43:21,800 --> 00:43:22,559
The Ma family's site...

1049
00:43:22,760 --> 00:43:23,239
There's trouble.

1050
00:43:24,199 --> 00:43:24,880
Come on, let me take that off for you.

1051
00:43:24,880 --> 00:43:25,760
Haven't eaten? Waiting for me?

1052
00:43:26,639 --> 00:43:27,599
Why are you pinching me?

1053
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:28,440
Listen to me,

1054
00:43:28,880 --> 00:43:30,199
there's trouble at our site.

1055
00:43:30,199 --> 00:43:30,840
Did you know?

1056
00:43:32,679 --> 00:43:34,360
My period is a few days late.

1057
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:35,960
I need to run back to work.

1058
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:37,760
Didn't you just get home?

1059
00:43:37,760 --> 00:43:38,840
Why are you leaving again?

1060
00:43:39,119 --> 00:43:40,400
Isn't anyone on duty today?

1061
00:43:40,519 --> 00:43:42,119
The doctor on duty just called me.

1062
00:43:42,400 --> 00:43:42,960
I'll be right back.

1063
00:43:44,679 --> 00:43:45,000
Wait for me.
